    "dominant_phase_unwrap": "RELIABLE",
    "model": "Radiated group delay (only with 11 points): H(f) = E_far(theta=0, phi=0, f) exp(+j k r) / a_inc(f), with a_inc the incident-wave voltage at the reference plane of the port (same plane as S11: launch plane for MSL edge ports, the lumped port itself for the vertical probe port: no plane shift, no beta), r = 1 m, k = 2 pi f / c0. E_theta and E_phi of the phi=0 cut are the x and y components at broadside (theta_hat = x_hat, phi_hat = y_hat at phi = 0). tau_g = -d arg(H)/d omega from the unwrapped phase with central differences (one-sided at the ends). The excitation spectrum and its phase cancel; the NF2FF phase centre only adds a constant (z of the centre / c0 at broadside). The absolute value contains the constant electrical length of the line and of the stub; only the variation over the band (ripple) is meaningful. DIAGNOSTIC: not validated against a reference; 49.92 MHz spacing is below the DTFT resolution 1/T_record of the run, so adjacent samples are not independent.",
    "reliability_criterion": "phase-unwrap reliability (round 12): a component is RELIABLE only if every wrapped phase step between adjacent frequency points is < pi/2 (1.5708 rad; the unwrap is unambiguous only below pi, pi/2 leaves a factor 2 margin; with 49.92 MHz spacing that is a residual delay < 5 ns) AND |H| >= -20 dB re its maximum over the points (a broadside null makes the phase jump by ~pi and the delay meaningless). Otherwise the component is UNRELIABLE and its delay values/ripple must not be used. The CSV columns reliable_* repeat the test per point (1 = both adjacent steps < pi/2 and |H| above the floor). Ripple (max - min of tau_g over the channel) is DIAGNOSTIC only: 11 correlated samples, one-sided end points, not validated.",
